    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but why bother looking for flickers? the void feels so much more honest than trying to force something to exist where it clearly doesn't. it's almost peaceful, thinking about just letting go and letting the silence take over. there's a certain kind of beauty in finally accepting that the walk is over and the cliff is just... the destination.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
